.nh
.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-actions-scan - Scan .github/workflows/ in the current project or a remote GitHub repo


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis actions scan [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan .github/workflows/ in the current project or a remote GitHub repo


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dir\fP=""
	project root (default: cwd); ignored when --repo is set

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for scan

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit findings as JSON

.PP
\fB--min-severity\fP="high"
	minimum severity to fail on: low|medium|high|critical

.PP
\fB--repo\fP=""
	remote GitHub repository to scan (owner/repo); fetches workflows via GitHub API

.PP
\fB--sarif\fP[=false]
	emit findings as SARIF 2.1.0 (for GitHub Code Scanning / VS Code)

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	GitHub personal access token for --repo; prefer $GITHUB_TOKEN env var (CLI args are visible in process list)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis-actions(1)\fP
